      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright represents the wizards; he views the cult as a dangerous corruption of magic and pushes aggressive arcane detection and lockdown measures.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright speaks for the Wizard\u2019s College on the council. (OBSERVED/CANON: role as head and representative of the arcane)\n\nHis angle on the cult is strongly interventionist: he sees the corrupted meat and the cult\u2019s actions as a perversion of magic and takes the threat very seriously. (CANON: loyalty/alignment context) In response, he advocates deploying Wizard\u2019s College resources\u2014magical detection (like runes to find corruption) and even a citywide magical lockdown\u2014to locate and counteract the cult\u2019s influence. (OBSERVED: goals)\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Head of the Wizard\u2019s College; arcane representative\n- Goals: Magical lockdown, detection runes, proactive countermeasures\n- Attitude toward cult: Sees it as dangerous, corrupt magic that must be rooted out quickly",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
