      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight **dead**\u2014specifically **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, with Bonogo taking the head.\n\nDespite earlier OBSERVED states showing the Wolf **\u201cDisappeared (became invisible)\u201d** and **attempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible**, the later OBSERVED outcome supersedes this: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** Bonogo\u2019s role confirms follow-through: **\u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d**  \nSo the escape attempt fails in the final state; the terminal outcome is death.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- physical_condition (OBSERVED): **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, previously Invisible\n- operational_status (OBSERVED): attempted escape via invisibility, but overridden by death\n- role (OBSERVED, Bonogo): **Removed the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it**\n- faction: cultist\n- rank_or_title: second-in-command of the guard\n\nNet: The Wolf is not at large\u2014he\u2019s dead, and in pieces.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_3",
      "question": "In that fight, is Thalia corrupted like the guards, or is it something different?",
