      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no evidence Thalia is corrupted like the guards; what\u2019s happening to her appears different and is not explicitly defined in the projection.\n\nBased on the available facts, **Guards** show clear signs of corruption: \u201cAll checked guards have an oily sheen to their eyes\u201d (OBSERVED), tied to the tainted meat and cult influence.  \n\nFor **Thalia**, the only relevant detail is that **the Wolf \u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d** (OBSERVED). There is **no mention of oily eyes, tainted meat effects, or other corruption markers** associated with her.\n\nGiven that distinction:\n- Guards = explicitly corrupted (observable physical signs, systemic cause).\n- Thalia = acting under influence or command, but **no confirmed corruption state**.\n\nSo in that fight, Thalia is **not confirmed corrupted like the guards**\u2014it\u2019s something else (likely influence, coercion, or manipulation), but the projection does not specify which.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Guards (OBSERVED): oily sheen in eyes; corruption linked to meat.\n- The Wolf (OBSERVED): issues commands, manipulates others.\n- Thalia: no recorded corruption indicators in context.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
