      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The council chamber itself fights back with arcane traps, environmental hazards, and sensory disruption\u2014especially punishing anyone without amulets.\n\n**Hazards in the Council Room**\n- **Arcane trap bursts** (CANON/OBSERVED): Deal **2d6 force damage** and can **temporarily paralyze** targets. These preferentially hit those **without amulets** (Players vs. Guards distinction).\n- **Trap targeting logic** (CANON): **Guards are exempt** via amulets; players may be singled out if they lack them.\n- **Falling debris** (OBSERVED): Forces players to **dodge falling debris hazards** and can knock them **thrown prone**.\n- **Illusory interference** (CANON): **Illusory walls/illusion spells** contribute to disorientation and mispositioning.\n- **Rune alarms** (OBSERVED): Trigger reinforcements and escalate pressure mid-fight.\n- **Ambient disruption** (CANON): Shifts in the chamber\u2019s **hum** signal changes; **echoing footsteps** hint at incoming threats, adding tension and misdirection.\n\n**Key Attributes**\n- Defenses: Arcane traps keyed to amulets; selective targeting.\n- Environment: Debris hazards; illusion magic.\n- Signals: Audible hum changes; echoing footsteps.\n- Security: Rune alarms tied to guard response.",
