      "answer": "TL;DR: Delay gives **the cult** time to advance their plan\u2014using hidden routes to sabotage, spread corruption, and potentially complete the flesh kaiju summoning\u2014while the **city\u2019s defenses and stability degrade**.\n\nIf the council stalls:\n- **Cult momentum (CANON/OBSERVED):** The cult is already active in the city and using hidden infrastructure; they can **access the heart of the city**, **sabotage or corrupt the cauldrons**, and **complete their summoning**.\n- **Hidden infiltration (CANON):** They rely on sewers and tunnels; blocking main routes won\u2019t stop them.\n- **Coordinated attacks (CANON):** The city is vulnerable to **coordinated attacks across the city**.\n- **Defense failure (CANON/OBSERVED):** The **integrity of the city\u2019s defenses is a concern**, and delay **brings the city closer to disaster**.\n- **Political rot (OBSERVED):** Cult influence in the council worsens outcomes if debate drags.\n- **Player risk (CANON/OBSERVED):** Ongoing delay + missing amulets = **traps may target them** while they\u2019re already **delayed by lengthy deliberation**.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: fragile, uneven fortification; proposed lockdown\n- Geography: sewers/hidden passages enable infiltration\n- Economy: festival-dependent (at risk)\n- Governance: divided council, cult influence present\n- Operational Status: escalating threat, nearing disaster",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
