      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room is a tense, partially chaotic aftermath\u2014guards on edge, signs of illusion magic, and the Wolf\u2019s body clearly shows the fight\u2019s outcome: \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d with lingering corruption clues like the oily sheen.\n\nThe room should feel disrupted but not destroyed. Illusory confusion likely left no lasting physical damage, but the **aftermath of deception** lingers\u2014people unsure what they saw was real.\n\nWhat stands out:\n- **The Wolf\u2019s corpse**: unmistakable\u2014\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d and noted corruption: \u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d\n- **Guards\u2019 posture**: surviving guards are **\u201cvisibly tense\u201d** and positioned defensively (a ring along the wall), reacting to alarms and the breach.\n- **Corruption tell**: multiple guards (and possibly the Wolf) share **\u201can oily sheen to their eyes,\u201d** reinforcing the hidden threat.\n- **Security response**: rune alarms have triggered; guards are actively containing the chamber.\n\nConflict note: Although the Wolf had escape attempts (invisibility/secret passage), the terminal state \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d is current and overrides escape outcomes.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Rune alarms active; guarded perimeter\n- Atmosphere: Tense, uncertain, post-deception\n- Clues: Oily sheen corruption; illusion aftermath\n- Geography: Secret escape tunnel beneath chamber (implied point of interest)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
