      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead at end of Session 12\u2014he was **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014and had shown clear signs of corruption before death.\n\n**State Resolution (OBSERVED):**\n- Physical condition includes **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, which is a terminal outcome and overrides earlier escape/invisibility states.\n- Bonogo\u2019s role confirms: **\u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d**\n- Prior to death, the Wolf had **\u201can oily sheen to his eyes,\u201d** indicating active corruption.\n\n**Conflict Note:**\n- OBSERVED operational status says he \u201cescapes\u201d and attempts to flee invisibly, but this is superseded by the later terminal outcome (decapitation). The death is the final state.\n\n**Key Attributes:**\n- Role: Enemy, saboteur, central adversary in council chamber\n- Faction: Cultist (sympathizer/agent)\n- Rank: Second-in-command of the guard\n- Defenses (CANON): Illusory duplicates\n- Mental state (pre-death): Desperate, regretful, begging for release/death\n\n**Conclusion:** Dead, formerly corrupted; corruption status is moot post-mortem.",
