      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive saboteur manipulating events; after, he is **Decapitated; head removed from body**, shifting from a scheming threat to a source of answers (via Speak with Dead).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Central adversary in the council chamber battle (CANON)\n- Rank: second-in-command of the guard (OBSERVED)\n- Faction: cultist / cult sympathizer (OBSERVED)\n\nBefore the fight (OBSERVED/CANON):\n- Operational: Actively deceiving the council, steering decisions, and attempting escape via invisibility and a secret tunnel.\n- Defenses: Uses illusory duplicates to confuse the party.\n- Mental state: Calculating but pressured; takes every opportunity to create confusion.\n- Loyalty: Betrayed Mirathorn; working to sabotage from within.\n\nAfter the fight (OBSERVED):\n- Physical: **Decapitated; head removed from body** (terminal outcome).\n- Operational: No longer an active threat; cannot escape or manipulate.\n- Narrative function: Becomes an information source (players plan Speak with Dead).\n- Mental shift (pre-death glimpse): desperate, regretful, even \u201cbegging to be killed.\u201d",
      "embedding_similarity": null
