      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was **played (ensorcelled), not corrupted**\u2014the Wolf was directly controlling/influencing her, which is why she acted against the party.\n\n**Explanation:**\n- **OBSERVED (Thalia):** She is explicitly *\u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d* and *\u201censorcelled (unbeknownst to her)\u201d*.  \n- **OBSERVED (Thalia physical):** *\u201cThalia does not have an oily sheen to her eyes.\u201d*  \n- **OBSERVED (Guards/Wolf):** The oily sheen is the marker of corruption tied to the wider cult influence.\n\nThis distinction matters:\n- **Corruption (oily sheen):** systemic, spreading influence (seen in guards and the Wolf).\n- **Ensorcellment (Thalia):** targeted manipulation by the Wolf.\n\n**Tie to the Wolf:**\n- The Wolf *\u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d* and is physically positioned *\u201cstanding at Thalia\u2019s shoulder.\u201d*\n- Thalia *\u201cserves the Wolf\u201d* during this period, but can be persuaded\u2014her *\u201cCharmed status ended\u201d* and she *\u201crealizes how dire the situation truly is.\u201d*\n\n**Conclusion:** Thalia wasn\u2019t inherently compromised\u2014she was a controlled asset. The Wolf used her authority as Commander to legitimize and extend his influence.\n\n**Key Attributes:**\n- **Thalia \u2013 Physical Condition:** No oily sheen; ensorcelled  \n- **Thalia \u2013 Loyalty Context:** Serves the Wolf (under influence), protective of city  \n- **Wolf \u2013 Role:** Manipulator, cult-aligned saboteur  \n- **Corruption Marker:** Oily sheen in eyes (absent in Thalia)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    }
